# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HydroDesk environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development. On Vercel, set these under
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables instead.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the application runs
# entirely in the browser using IndexedDB, which is why it deploys without any
# configuration at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres connection string. Setting this switches project storage from the
# browser to the database, which is what makes projects visible across devices
# and makes read-only share links possible.
#
# This is a real secret. It is read only on the server, inside API routes, and
# never reaches the browser. Do not prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — anything with
# that prefix is compiled into the client bundle and is readable by anyone.
#
# Get one free from https://neon.tech (Project -> Connection string -> pooled).
# The schema is created automatically on first use; there is no migration to run.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
